TASK-513 regression fixture — a saved (trimmed, but structurally faithful) PubMed
efetch XML response. Mirrors the real shape that caused the wrong-DOI bug: each
PubmedArticle carries its OWN doi under PubmedData/ArticleIdList, but ALSO carries a
PubmedData/ReferenceList where every cited Reference has its OWN nested ArticleIdList
with a DIFFERENT doi. A naive ".//ArticleIdList/ArticleId" search matches both and can
return the cited paper's doi instead of the article's own.

  - PMID 11111111 (Article A): has its own doi via ArticleIdList; ReferenceList carries
    two unrelated reference DOIs that must NEVER be returned.
  - PMID 22222222 (Article B): has NO doi anywhere (no ArticleIdList doi, no ELocationID
    doi) but its ReferenceList reference DOES have a doi — must resolve to None, not the
    borrowed reference doi.
  - PMID 33333333 (Article C): has no PubmedData/ArticleIdList doi entry, but the
    article's own ELocationID carries EIdType="doi" — exercises the fallback path.
-->
